  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors II: testing three points for collinearity</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.6: Find AB and BC for three points in three dimensions and decide whether the points are collinear.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 7 in Exercise D of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: collinear and non-collinear cases with a stated verdict, new points, randomised over a curated list, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
